      "worked": "Let $P(x)=3x^3+ax^2+bx-6$. By the factor theorem, $P(-2)=0$ and $P(3)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=3(-2)^3+a(-2)^2+b(-2)-6\\\\P(-2)&=4a-2b-30\\\\4a-2b-30&=0\\\\2a-b&=15\\qquad(1)\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}P(3)&=3(3)^3+a(3)^2+b(3)-6\\\\P(3)&=9a+3b+75\\\\9a+3b+75&=0\\\\3a+b&=-25\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nAdd equations (1) and (2), then substitute into (1).\n$$\\begin{align*}(2a-b)+(3a+b)&=15-25\\\\5a&=-10\\\\a&=-2\\\\2(-2)-b&=15\\\\-b&=19\\\\b&=-19\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
